{"data": {"notes": [], "reqs": [{"kind": "contract", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R1", "source": {"type": "task_metadata"}, "status": "active", "text": "Entry point `solve` in language python, within the stated limits.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R2", "source": {"char_end": 1384, "char_start": 0, "quote": "You are an expert Python programmer. You will be given a question (problem specification) and will generate a correct Python program that matches the specification and passes all tests.\n\n### Question:\nYou are given a string s consisting only of digits. A valid pair is defined as two adjacent digits in s such that:\n\nThe first digit is not equal to the second.\nEach digit in the pair appears in s exactly as many times as its numeric value.\n\nReturn the first valid pair found in the string s when traversing from left to right. If no valid pair exists, return an empty string.\n \nExample 1:\n\nInput: s = \"2523533\"\nOutput: \"23\"\nExplanation:\nDigit '2' appears 2 times and digit '3' appears 3 times. Each digit in the pair \"23\" appears in s exactly as many times as its numeric value. Hence, the output is \"23\".\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput: s = \"221\"\nOutput: \"21\"\nExplanation:\nDigit '2' appears 2 times and digit '1' appears 1 time. Hence, the output is \"21\".\n\nExample 3:\n\nInput: s = \"22\"\nOutput: \"\"\nExplanation:\nThere are no valid adjacent pairs.\n\n \nConstraints:\n\n2 <= s.length <= 100\ns only consists of digits from '1' to '9'.\n\n### Format: You will use the following starter code to write the solution to the problem and enclose your code within delimiters.\n```python\nclass Solution:\n    def findValidPair(self, s: str) -> str:\n        \n```\n\n### Answer: (use the provided format with backticks)\n\n", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "The program is correct on all legal inputs of the statement.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R3", "source": {"char_end": 1425, "char_start": 1396, "quote": "Input:\n\"2523533\"\nOutput:\n\"23\"", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 1: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R4", "source": {"char_end": 1462, "char_start": 1437, "quote": "Input:\n\"221\"\nOutput:\n\"21\"", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 2: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R5", "source": {"char_end": 1496, "char_start": 1474, "quote": "Input:\n\"22\"\nOutput:\n\"\"", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 3: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}], "request_sha": "b614828d735c182f1ce53991f12bf341fd8bf016f70b1ffde64a512b9a081b34", "stop": null}, "kind": "requirements", "prev": "281d63615e5adefc5a9cb6626625e46a7d31e3c361c627397fe43d06a9a7fdff", "seq": 2}
